  "aiContextParagraph": "The proposal by DPD RI Chair Sultan Najamudin to increase the number of vice presidents to three has drawn significant attention across Indonesian political circles. According to the DPD RI Chair, the idea is intended as a long-term strategic discussion rather than a proposal for the current administration. He emphasized that the suggestion should be viewed as a comprehensive concept rather than an attempt to create political sensation. However, the proposal has encountered skepticism from various political figures, including Bambang Pacul, and raised questions regarding its urgency and practical application within the current political structure of the country. This discourse occurs alongside the DPD RI leadership's active engagement in broader national issues, including support for the multilateral diplomatic efforts led by President Prabowo Subianto during the APEC Summit in China and the pursuit of national economic targets.",
